; Leg HH -- the FreeDOS console arm.  The Victor leg has NO REDIRECT.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
; THE VICTOR SIDE OF THIS LEG HAS NO REDIRECT AND NO --nodisplay, AND THAT IS
; THE POINT.  SS16u: the transfer display goes away under the redirect that
; records the counters, so a leg that has to SHOW you a screen cannot have
; one.  SS16ba's first attempt and SS16az leg FDG both died of this.
;
; THERE ARE THEREFORE NO COUNTERS FROM THIS LEG.  HG is the run with the
; counters; this is the run with the picture.  PHOTOGRAPH THE SCREEN
; MID-TRANSFER.
;
; What is being verified: SS1g's ANSI arm, chosen by the same INT 21h AH=30h
; probe that picks the IRQ1 vector.  victor_ansi.asm:154 passes anything that
; is not ESC [ straight to the screen, so a VT52 display would PRINT a Y and
; two coordinate bytes 55 times a repaint.
;
; SS16az leg FDA's screen garbage was read as ours and is RETRACTED:
; victor_trace.c writes the KERNEL's debug region to screen rows 12-24.
; Nothing distinguishes our output from the kernel's on rows 12-24.  Read
; the top of the screen.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPHH.OUT> s16bcHH.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bcHH.pkt
send rcvhh.dat
statistics
